{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-4084","published":"2026-09-25T01:28:13Z","modified":"2026-09-25T01:45:10.352253245Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-12080"],"summary":"qemu security update","details":"QEMU is a FAST! processor emulator using dynamic translation to achieve good emulation speed.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA flaw was found in the QEMU Guest Agent (qga). A local unprivileged user can exploit a vulnerability in the guest-ssh-add-authorized-keys command handler by manipulating symbolic links. This can occur either through a deterministic directory-symlink bypass or a Time-of-Check to Time-of-Use (TOCTOU) file-symlink race. Successful exploitation allows the attacker to gain ownership of arbitrary root-owned files or directories, leading to root access. This vulnerability requires an external management layer (e.g., libvirt) to trigger the affected code path.(CVE-2026-12080)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"qemu","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/qemu&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.2.0-89.oe2403sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["qemu-8.2.0-89.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qemu-block-curl-8.2.0-89.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qemu-block-iscsi-8.2.0-89.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qemu-block-rbd-8.2.0-89.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qemu-block-ssh-8.2.0-89.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qemu-debuginfo-8.2.0-89.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qemu-debugsource-8.2.0-89.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qemu-guest-agent-8.2.0-89.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qemu-hw-usb-host-8.2.0-89.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qemu-img-8.2.0-89.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qemu-system-aarch64-8.2.0-89.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qemu-system-arm-8.2.0-89.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qemu-system-riscv-8.2.0-89.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qemu-system-x86_64-8.2.0-89.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qemu-user-8.2.0-89.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qemu-user-binfmt-8.2.0-89.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qemu-user-static-8.2.0-89.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["q